{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\np='update.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['investigations']=d.get('investigations',[])\nd['investigations'].append({\n \\\"ref\\\":\\\"@understate\\\",\\\"id\\\":None,\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"When RestoreCommittedLogs makes a restarted leader forget a voter whose addition is committed in its own log, does the resulting smaller in-memory quorum let it accept and apply entries that only a minority of the committed voters hold?\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"append_config_entry\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\"],\n \\\"parent_id\\\":\\\"9c549c026d7341f2b1e328826eac6dc3-question-0\\\",\n \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"Yes: with the added voter D absent from the restarted leader's configuration, its quorum is two of {A,B,C} instead of three of {A,B,C,D}, so a partition that leaves only A and B connected still lets it commit and apply an entry, and the client is told the write succeeded although a quorum of the committed configuration never received it.\\\",\n \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"Four voters {A,B,C}+D added after a snapshot, further commits, then restart the leader with the flag on and off; partition C and D from A and apply one entry. Prediction with the flag: the Apply succeeds and only A and B hold the entry; prediction without the flag: the same partition makes the Apply fail.\\\",\n \\\"disposition\\\":\\\"active\\\"})\nd['experiment']={\n \\\"investigation_id\\\":\\\"@understate\\\",\n \\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"assurance_understate_test.go\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"newraft_scan\\\",\\\"restore_committed\\\",\\\"snapshot_config\\\",\\\"append_config_entry\\\",\\\"next_configuration\\\",\\\"commit_config_on_append\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Four in-process nodes at protocol version 3 with 50ms timeouts. A is bootstrapped with voters {A,B,C}, all four run, A snapshots, commits a command, adds D as a voter (committed configuration {A,B,C,D}, quorum three) and commits two further commands. A is restarted on the same stores with RestoreCommittedLogs (case restore_on) or without it (control restore_off), with the other three nodes' timeouts lengthened so the restarted leader wins its re-election. The probe records the restarted leader's configuration against the others, then partitions C and D from A and applies one entry, recording whether the Apply succeeded, the entry index, A's commit and applied indexes, each voter's log tail, and how many of the four committed voters hold the entry.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"D is caught up before the restart, so the committed configuration genuinely has four voters (quorum three).\\\",\\\"C and D are disconnected in both directions, which is a real partition for all Raft traffic; A and B remain connected.\\\",\\\"The committed configuration {A,B,C,D} requires three acknowledgements, so an entry held by A and B only is not committed under it.\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"No disk faults or message loss; the only partition is the explicit disconnection of C and D.\\\",\\\"D is kept on the normal restart path (flag disabled) so its own configuration recovery cannot confound the observation.\\\"],\n  \\\"parameters\\\":{\\\"protocol_version\\\":3,\\\"voters\\\":4,\\\"heartbeat_timeout_ms\\\":50,\\\"election_timeout_ms\\\":50}},\n \\\"prefix\\\":\\\"Real bootstrap, real snapshot, real AddVoter with catch-up, real commits, real shutdown and restart of the leader on the same InmemCommitTrackingStore/InmemStore/InmemSnapshotStore instances, real transport partition. Nothing is fabricated.\\\",\n \\\"prerequisites\\\":[\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_und_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_und_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"before_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_und_write_on\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_setup_restore_on\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_on\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_is_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]},\n  {\\\"alias\\\":\\\"admit_und_write_off\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_setup_restore_off\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"mode\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"restore_off\\\"},{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_is_leader\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True}]}\n ],\n \\\"comparisons\\\":[\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_restart_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_und_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A restarted leader must not forget a voter whose addition is committed in its own log.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"after_restart_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_und_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"a_servers\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":4},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: the same restart without RestoreCommittedLogs keeps all four voters.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_write_restore_on\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_und_write_on\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"entry_on_committed_quorum\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"An entry whose Apply reported success must be held by a quorum of the configuration committed in the log, which has four voters and requires three.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_write_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_und_write_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"write_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed four-voter configuration the same partition must make the leader refuse the write.\\\"}\n ]\n}\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['limitations'].append(\\\"A third consequence direction is being probed: a restarted node that forgets an added voter holds a smaller quorum than the committed configuration, and a construction-time run of that harness accepted a write held by only two of four committed voters while the control refused it; its retained receipt is requested in this update.\\\")\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
