st be held by a quorum of the configuration committed in the log, which has four voters and requires three.\\\"},\n  {\\\"event\\\":\\\"split_write_restore_off\\\",\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"mode\\\"],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"admit_und_write_off\\\",\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"write_applied\\\",\\\"op\\\":\\\"eq\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Control: with the committed four-voter configuration the same partition must make the leader refuse the write.\\\"}\n ]\n}\npar=d['interpretations'][0]\npar['limitations'].append(\\\"A third consequence direction is being probed: a restarted node that forgets an added voter holds a smaller quorum than the committed configuration, and a construction-time run of that harness accepted a write held by only two of four committed voters while the control refused it; its retained receipt is requested in this update.\\\")\njson.dump(d, open(p,'w'), indent=2)\nEOF\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_09-22-37-hashicorp_raft-real-run; /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run . --submission update.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"af7ab1df563f4f5686eb47935464cf57\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 1931.3303875810002, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": true}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Pursued the last sourced lead on the decision-formation axis and reproduced it: a restarted node that forgets a voter whose addition is committed in its own log holds a smaller quorum than the committed configuration. In the four-voter probe (bootstrap {A,B,C}, AddVoter D committed, then restart the leader with RestoreCommittedLogs) the restarted leader reports three servers while the other nodes report four, and after partitioning C and D from A a single Apply succeeds — A commits and applies the entry at index 8 while C sits at 7 and D at 6, so only two of the four committed voters hold it; the control without the flag refuses the same write ('leadership lost while committing log'). This is a distinct direction from the resurrected-voter case (understated rather than resurrected membership) and it is registered as a second child of the same question with four comparisons; the harness is self-contained, verified in an isolated copy of the captured tree, and fresh execution is requested. The parent interpretation notes the pending receipt.\"}"}}
